From 91cb8bfb71ed74027467dbe565a77de0d8b279ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:46:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] portability: cmsis_rtos_v1: call thread function through
 os_pthread

zephyr_thread_wrapper() calls the user's thread function, an os_pthread,
through a pointer of type void *(*)(void *). os_pthread is
void (*)(void const *): the return types differ, so the call is through an
incompatible function type, which is undefined behaviour.

Most targets tolerate it. Targets that check the type of indirect calls do
not: WebAssembly traps on the call, and so would a CFI-enabled build.
Declare the pointer as os_pthread, the type osThreadDef stores it as.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APoUNc1caCDU2PVRFEQRyi
---
 subsys/portability/cmsis_rtos_v1/cmsis_thread.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/subsys/portability/cmsis_rtos_v1/cmsis_thread.c b/subsys/portability/cmsis_rtos_v1/cmsis_thread.c
index d90780d39e8..391ecbd4b65 100644
--- a/subsys/portability/cmsis_rtos_v1/cmsis_thread.c
+++ b/subsys/portability/cmsis_rtos_v1/cmsis_thread.c
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ static void zephyr_thread_wrapper(void *arg1, void *arg2, void *arg3)
 {
 	ARG_UNUSED(arg2);
 
-	void * (*fun_ptr)(void *) = arg3;
+	os_pthread fun_ptr = arg3;
 
 	fun_ptr(arg1);
 }
